the federal government is hitting the  pause button tonight on what could be  one of the biggest and most  consequential technology deals ever it  involves an American company and the  administration concerned that a hostile  foreign takeover could jeopardize  American leadership in a critical  industry correspondent Julian Turner  looks at what a stake at stake rather in  that deal tonight we will stand up to  any country that unlawfully forces  American companies to transfer their  valuable technology as the worldwide  race to develop 5g the fifth generation  of wireless technology heats up a single  takeover deal is threatening to  undermine America's competitive edge in  the tech sector and jeopardize its  national security interests San  diego-based Qualcomm is currently  leading the pack when it comes to 5g  research and development but a  Singaporean company called Broadcom is  now making a bid to acquire Qualcomm for  a staggering 117 billion dollars one of  the largest deals the tech sector has  ever seen experts now warn that were the  deal to go through  Qualcomm America's leader in telecoms  would be forced out of the 5g race  handing a victory to its Chinese  competitors Americans should be  concerned that if China does this then  first of all they are going to dominate  global communications in the wireless  area but also that they will be able to  spy on Americans because 5g will connect  many devices in their homes but 5g  technology isn't just for your TV or  your phone it'll be used in the future  for self-driving cars and wireless  virtual reality the Trump  administration's Committee on foreign  investment in the United States known as  Sophia's is now intervened putting the  deal on hold for one month while it  undertakes a review saying quote any  other potential merger between Broadcom  and Qualcomm could pose a risk to the  national security of the United States  some senior lawmakers are also concerned  about the risks China has made it no  secret they have a national strategy  they've announced it they're  implementing it too  vacuum up startup technology companies  and other companies that produce dual  use technology that has national  security implications a former national  security official who's familiar with  Qualcomm tells FOX News that should this  deal go through it effectively forfeit  the future of American 5g bill Thank You  Gillian
 

